Many of you may have spent the past few weeks exchanging gifts with family and friends, and maybe you're now enjoying some new possessions, or returning those that didn't fit or weren't quite what you wanted. Perhaps you're going through your old stuff, following through on a New Year's resolution to declutter. So it seems like a good time of year to talk about possessions and what possessions mean to us. The things we own can be central to our identity, according to some researchers, part of how we see ourselves and how other people see us.
你们中的许多人可能在过去几周里与家人和朋友交换了礼物，也许现在正享受着新物品带来的快乐，或者正在退掉那些不合身或不尽如人意的礼物。也许你正在整理旧物，践行新年清理杂物的决心。因此，现在似乎是一年之中谈论“拥有物”以及它们对我们意味着什么的绝佳时机。一些研究人员认为，我们拥有的东西可能是我们身份的核心，是我们看待自己以及他人看待我们方式的一部分。

