or streaming movies. Rather, we get an image of an artwork or an image of an avatar and we don't own the original, and we don't have the same sort of ownership rights that we would have if we do have, or did have, or own the original. There's another aspect to that, and that is that the artist can get some residual rights when our digital token is sold at a higher price, and they can get a claim, often 10% of that increase in value. And this goes back to an old 1972 auction of the skull collection in New York. And this was a collection of expressionist and pop art. And it was one where the auction was filmed. And there were also discussions between the artists and the collectors and some of the buyers.
或流媒体电影那样的访问权限。相反，我们得到的是一件艺术品的图像或一个化身的图像，我们并不拥有原件，也没有我们拥有或曾经拥有原件时所享有的那种所有权。这还有另一个方面，那就是当我们的数字代币以更高的价格出售时，艺术家可以获得一些剩余权利，他们可以获得索赔权，通常是增值部分的10%。这可以追溯到1972年纽约斯卡尔（Skull）收藏品的拍卖会。这是一场表现主义和波普艺术的收藏。拍卖过程被拍摄了下来。艺术家、收藏家和一些买家之间也进行了讨论。

